      },
      {
        "id": "p62-q1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$AB$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$14.8\\text{ m}$\n\nFind $AO$ and $BO$ using the elevation triangles, then use Pythagoras’ theorem in $AOB$.",
          "worked": "Use the unrounded height $OH=10\\sin35^\\circ$.\n$$\\begin{align*}AO&=10\\cos35^\\circ\\\\BO&=\\frac{OH}{\\tan25^\\circ}\\\\BO&=\\frac{10\\sin35^\\circ}{\\tan25^\\circ}.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $\\angle AOB=90^\\circ$,\n$$\\begin{align*}AB^2&=AO^2+BO^2\\\\AB&=\\sqrt{(10\\cos35^\\circ)^2+\\left(\\frac{10\\sin35^\\circ}{\\tan25^\\circ}\\right)^2}\\\\AB&\\approx14.8\\text{ m}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 70
      }
    ]
